Author: clever-wolf-203 <clever-wolf-203@invalid>
Date:   Sun Nov 15 17:28:31 2026 +0000

    live_deploy: OidcConfigArtifact is an installed artifact; serve declares reading its config
    
    Manager-approved (msg msg_26b106e3): model (A) + (1), with the correction that a non-unit must never be
    carried as NotYetModeled (that label means "unit whose reads aren't modeled yet" — a false TODO for a config
    document).
    
    - closure: ArtifactReadSet gains a truthful InstalledArtifact arm (a non-executable artifact the deploy
      installs, read by the units that declare it). It is NEVER in the gate population (enable legs only), so it
      is never consulted as a unit's read; its inventory row InstalledArtifactRow keeps it located and countable.
    - adapter: OidcConfigArtifact => InstalledArtifact (was the false NotYetModeled). The serve unit (SystemdUnit)
      read-set now GAINS the OIDC config path it reads at startup, sourced from deployment_oidc_config_steps — the
      SAME authority that installs the OidcConfigArtifact (its path is tracker_web placement cfg.config_path) — so
      serve's read and the owned artifact are one string, never a second spelling (single_authority). When OIDC is
      unplaced the list is empty and serve reads no config, exactly as the emitted unit carries no OIDC Environment.
    
    Controls (base-matched seed sha256 900599bd...):
    - the_serve_unit_read_set_includes_the_oidc_config_it_reads: the serve read-set contains the INSTALLED
      OidcConfigArtifact step's path (srv1 has OIDC placed; Absent => false, not a decoration).
    - the_oidc_config_artifact_is_an_installed_artifact_not_a_reader: its row maps to InstalledArtifactRow, never
      Declared/Unclosed.
    - regressions inventory_maps / every_enabled_step / a_fresh_host / roster PASS.
    
    Node: deploy-intent-owns-artifact-closure (node://adhoc-3e6e9bfb-d59).

